        "comment_corrections": [
          [
            "How many rows each provider can produce, for the start-up report and the tests:",
            "Material-level coverage estimates for diagnostics, not counts of all runtime or viewer rows:"
          ],
          [
            "GT6 carries the tier in the tile entity ({@code MultiTileEntityHDDSwitch.mUSBTier}); an item has\n     * no tile entity, and the port registers exactly one item per drive tier, so the id <em>is</em> the\n     * tier. Documented rather than hidden: a renamed item would silently stop being a drive.",
            "This helper parses the registry path; selected-file readers apply separate file-tier gates.\n     * The native USB switch instead recognizes built-in media through {@code UsbDataMedia}."
          ],
          [
            "rebuilds the material: gem → gem plate → ingot → plate → nugget (9) → chunk (4) → dust → tiny\n *       dust (9) → small dust (4) → stick (2), and its fluid when it has no such form.",
            "rebuilds the material, preferring its ambient fluid, then its priority prefix, then gem → gem\n *       plate → ingot → plate → nugget (9) → chunk (4) → dust → tiny dust (9) → small dust (4)\n *       → stick (2), with liquid/gas/plasma fallback when no item form is available."
          ]
        ],
